    {
      "id": "be-s6-demand-functions-c1",
      "heading": "Interpreting a demand function",
      "explanation_md": "A demand function is a **mathematical representation of a demand curve**. The slide's example:\n\n**Qd = 10 - 2PX + 3PY - 2M**\n\nRead the **sign of each coefficient**:\n\n- Coefficient of **PX is negative** (-2): the **law of demand holds**.\n- Coefficient of **PY is positive** (+3): **X and Y are substitutes**.\n- Coefficient of **M is negative** (-2): **X is an inferior good**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-s6-demand-fn-signs"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Signs in Qd = 10 - 2PX + 3PY - 2M: PX negative (law of demand), PY positive (substitutes), M negative (inferior good).",
      "clarification": null,
