    {
      "id": "be-s6-demand-functions-c3",
      "heading": "Log-linear demand: the coefficients are the elasticities",
      "explanation_md": "The **general log-linear demand function** is:\n\n**ln Qd = β0 + βX ln PX + βY ln PY + βM ln M + βH ln H**\n\nHere the elasticities **are the coefficients**:\n\n- **Own price elasticity = βX**\n- **Cross price elasticity = βY**\n- **Income elasticity = βM**\n\n**Example:** ln(Qd) = 10 - 2 ln(P). Own price elasticity = **-2**, everywhere along the curve.\n\nGraph: the slide draws **linear demand** and **log-linear demand** side by side, each as a demand curve D with P against Q.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-s6-loglinear-example"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Log-linear: the coefficients on ln P, ln PY and ln M are the own price, cross price and income elasticities. ln(Qd) = 10 - 2 ln(P) gives -2.",
